    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "This substantial double-fronted family home enjoys a spacious and sunny SW facing back garden, accessed by a wide side passage. It is set on a quiet cul-de-sac in a highly desirable location off Butterfield Avenue in Rathfarnham, close to a superb range of schools, parks, shops, The Old Orchard pub, and other local amenities, It has a lovely large sunroom to the rear where it is not overlooked, making a delightful play or relaxation space.\n\nAccommodation consists of an entrance hall leading to a well proportioned living room, a spacious kitchen dining room. Double doors open from the kitchen to a very large, bright, SW facing sunroom with a lofted ceiling 3.5m high. A door off the hall leads to a garage conversion room which could make an excellent playroom, home office, or 5th bedroom. Immediately behind this is a downstairs shower room accessed from the utility room to the rear.\n\nThe generous back garden is about 60ft long and 40ft wide. It is SW facing and flooded with sunlight from mid morning to sunset. \n\nThe front garden has a driveway with off-street parking for two cars.There is a triangular shaped front lawn with a fence along one side. On the other side of that fence is the driveway to 7a which was built in the side garden of #7. There is a gap of almost 3 metres between the two houses.. \n\nTo the rear of #7 is a roofless block-built shed which could either be demolished to give more garden space or reinstated if you need the storage. This was originally a garage/workshop before vehicular access was cut off when 7a was built in the side garden."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Entrance hall - 6.74m (22'1\") x 3.06m (10'0\")\nComposite triple-locking front door. Large window to front. Carpet tiles. Doors to living room, kitchen and downstairs bedroom.\n\nLliving room - 4.25m (13'11\") x 4.1m (13'5\")\nWell proportioned room with large double-glazed window to front, coving and centre rose. Wood laminate flooring. Curtains and curtain rod. Closed off chimney.\n\nKitchen/.dining room - 7.17m (23'6\") x 3.65m (12'0\")\nSpacious room with double-doors and a window opening to the sunroom. Wood laminate flooring. Fitted kitchen. Door to utility room.\n\nSunroom - 8.14m (26'8\") x 3.41m (11'2\")\nSW facing sunroom opening to the back garden. A lovely bright space flooded with natural sunlight all afternoon and evening. Pine panelled, lofted ceiling 3.5m high, with exposed beams. Double-glazed windows on three sides. Glazed door to back garden. Recessed lighting. Two skyl;ights.\n\nUtility room - 3.6m (11'10\") x 2.37m (7'9\")\nDoor to back garden. Door to downstairs shower room. Plumbed for washing machine and dryer. Hot press 1.3m x 0.8m.\n\nDownstairs shower room - 2.62m (8'7\") x 2.34m (7'8\")\nGlass shower cubicle. Frosted glass window. WC. WHB. Door to utility room. This room is immediately behind the downstairs bedroom making it quite easy to turn it into an ensuite if needed.\n\nDownstairs study / playroom - 4.08m (13'5\") x 2.36m (7'9\")\nLarge window to front. Door from hall. Carpet tiles.\n\nLanding - 6.25m (20'6\") x 1.1m (3'7\")\nCarpet. Window on one end. Attic access hatch.\n\nMain bedroom - 5.27m (17'3\") x 4.1m (13'5\")\nGenerous room with two windows. Door to ensuite. Finished pine floorboards. Curtains and curtain rods.\n\nensuite - 2.41m (7'11\") x 1.74m (5'9\")\nTiled shower cubicle with Triton electric shower. Frosted glass window. WC. WHB. Outside vent.\n\nBedroom 2 - 4.4m (14'5\") x 3.62m (11'11\")\nSpacious double bedroom. Carpet. Curtain rod.\n\nBedroom 3 - 4.32m (14'2\") x 3.38m (11'1\")\nL shaped room with wardrobe. Window to front. Carpet.\n\nBedroom 4 - 4.47m (14'8\") x 2.44m (8'0\")\nWindow to front. Curtain rod. Carpet.\n\nBathroom - 2.41m (7'11\") x 2.32m (7'7\")\nBathtub with glass shower screen and wall mounted shower. Tiled walls. WC. WHB. Frosted glass window to rear.\n\nBack garden - 17.4m (57'1\") x 11.7m (38'5\")\nSpacious SW facing back garden. back lawn. Roofless block built garden shed. side access.\n\nFront garden - 12m (39'4\") x 11.7m (38'5\")\nOff-street parking for two cars. Triangular shaped front lawn. Side gate.\n\nNotice\nIntending purchasers must satisfy themselves as to the accuracy\nof all information and measurements in this listing. Any particulars\nprovided are for guidance only and do not constitute a contract or a part of\none. We do not accept responsibility for any loss or damage arising from\nreliance on this information. Purchasers should seek independent legal and\nprofessional advice."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li> Spacious and sunny SW facing back garden </li><li> Large sunroom </li><li> Quiet cul-de-sac off Butterfield Avenue </li><li> Desirable area with spacious family homes </li><li> Side passage 1.65m wide. There is almost a 3m gap between #7 & 7a </li><li> Freehold property with no service charge </li><li> Highly regarded local schools </li><li> Close to Rathfarnham Shopping Centre and The Old Orchard </li><li> Footpath to Bushy Park via Dodder footbridge </li><li> Served by bus routes S6 and 15B</li></ul>"
